@jonathanhefner,

1) It works with a forward slash.

2) Yes, if I add another test file and use the command with backslash, both test files will be run.

@heynan0 Thank you for verifying!

The cause of this issue is that the test runner only considers an argument to be a file path [if it contains a forward slash](https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/ab18f60841c11427948be444ee5ff0008fd4c3fb/railties/lib/rails/test_unit/runner.rb#L83-L85).  The fix would be to also recognize back slashes.  However, this might open up a can of worms.  Ruby (and Windows) can typically handle either slash without problems, but I'm not sure if there are other parts of Rails that expect forward slashes only when processing paths.

@kaspth  What do you think about this?  Should I create a PR to accept Windows-style paths in the test runner?
